.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Defines a typed, fixed‑stride buffer abstraction for unmanaged element types\&. 

\fRITypeBuffer<T>\fP represents a simple, element‑oriented view over a raw byte buffer (for example a \fR\fBCache\fP\fP)\&. Implementations expose element access, cloning, clearing and fill semantics for unmanaged value types\&. All conversions between \fIT\fP  and the underlying bytes are the responsibility of the concrete implementation\&. 

.PP
The interface intentionally keeps the surface small and portable: implementations may perform endian conversion, bounds validation, and copy semantics as required by the runtime\&. 

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP An unmanaged value type stored in the buffer\&.
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBType Constraints\fP
.TP
\fIT\fP : \fIunmanaged\fP
.PP
